{"text": "= Fax(212)481-3516\n\n970 Lexington Ave., New York, N.Y. 10017\n\nPhone (212)685-9773\n\nTranslation from Italian\n\nRe:\n\nb/mr\n\nIl Mattino, December 19, 1994\n\nLONDON\n\"Passive smoking?\nIt's not harmful,\n\nBut it is controversial.\nLONDON. Passive smoking is not the end of the world; it\napparently causes minimal damage, comparable to that sustained\nby anyone who inhales one cigarette per week. That is what is\nmaintained by an independent research laboratory - Hazleton\nBurope- headquartered in Harrogate in Eastern England. The\nscientists of the British laboratory took a sampling of 255\nnonsmokers, submitted them for 24 hours to passive smoking and\nconducted saliva and urine tests. The research indicates that\nPassive smoking is trivial compared to other sources of air\nPollution. The opinion of Hazleton Europe is opposite that of\n\nthe British Health Ministry.\n\nPLLz8zE\u00a207",
